tes within astrocytes in demyelinating lesions</article-title><source>J Neuropathol Exp Neurol</source><year>1992</year><volume>51</volume><fpage>40</fpage><lpage>46</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1740673</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wu</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Brosnan</surname><given-names>CF</given-names></name><name><surname>Raine</surname><given-names>CS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>SP40,40 immunoreactivity in inflammatory CNS lesions displaying astrocyte/oligodendrocyte interactions</article-title><source>J Neuropathol Exp  Neurol</source><year>1993</year><volume>52</volume><fpage>129</fpage><lpage>134</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8440994</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Raine</surname><given-names>CS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Norton lecture: a review of the oligodendrocyte in the multiple sclerosis lesion</article-title><source>J Neuroimmunol</source><year>1997</year><volume>77</volume><fpage>135</fpage><lpage>152</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9258244</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><label>28</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rogers</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Gasque</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Piddlesden</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Okada</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Holers</surname><given-names>VM</given-names></name><name><surname>Morgan</surname><given-names>BP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Expression and function of membrane regulators of complement on rat astrocytes in culture</article-title><source>Immunology</source><year>1